# PROPOSAL 3 — Re-typed addressbook affordance descriptor (DO NOT APPLY; review)
#
# Target (live, MUST NOT be modified by this exercise):
#   https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/affordances/org-find-by-ror.ttl
#   source: overlays/addressbook/affordances/org-find-by-ror.ttl
#
# Audit finding addressed: WARN descriptor:untyped — catalog entry was typed
# only wiki:Affordance, escaping the prof:ResourceDescriptor contract (no
# prof:hasRole / rdfs:label / dct:conformsTo / wiki:installedBy enforced).
#
# Fix: add 'a prof:ResourceDescriptor', prof:hasRole wikirole:query-affordance
# (NEW role — see proposal-2), rdfs:label, dct:conformsTo <PROF spec>, and
# wiki:installedBy <overlay#addressbook>. The existing sh:agentInstruction and
# wiki:selectQuery are preserved verbatim. These descriptors are SPARQL query
# surfaces (selectQuery run client-side), NOT ?ext= HTTP dispatch, so they are
# modeled as wikirole:query-affordance, NOT wiki:SearchAffordance.
#
# Lands in overlays/addressbook/affordances/org-find-by-ror.ttl so 'make reset'
# reproduces it; the addressbook manifest already lists this affordance.

@prefix wiki:     <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wiki#> .
@prefix sh:       <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dct:      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prof:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/dx/prof/> .
@prefix wikirole: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wikirole#> .

</vault/meta/affordances/org-find-by-ror.ttl>
    a wiki:Affordance ,
       prof:ResourceDescriptor ;
    prof:hasRole wikirole:query-affordance ;
    rdfs:label "Organization lookup by ROR" ;
    dct:conformsTo <http://www.w3.org/TR/dx-prof/> ;
    wiki:installedBy <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/overlay#addressbook> ;
    sh:agentInstruction """
      Canonical institutional identity lookup via ROR (Research Organization
      Registry) IRI. Use this when an external source provides a ROR identifier
      (e.g., from a funding record or ORCID affiliation) and you need the local
      Organization card.

      Parameter: $ror — the full ROR IRI as a named node, e.g.,
      <https://ror.org/00mkhxb43> (University of Notre Dame).
      Pass the angle-bracketed form in SPARQL; the affordance engine substitutes
      it as an IRI.

      Sources: Organization cards at /vault/contacts/Organization/*/index.ttl.
      Enumerate via LDP listing of </vault/contacts/Organization/> or use
      Comunica link-traversal with the Organization container as entry point.

      Returns 0..1 ?org IRIs. Zero means no Organization card exists for this
      ROR; the agent should prompt to create a stub card via the addressbook
      overlay templates.
    """ ;
    wiki:selectQuery """
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>

SELECT ?org WHERE {
  ?org owl:sameAs $ror .
}
    """ .
